+
+## Pre-merge receipt v2 and classification provenance
+
+The final pre-merge revision supersedes the prototype v1 receipt representation.
+`expression-research-run-v2` retains the same exact consumed values as sparse
+`session_input_deltas`, with `session_input_hashes`. `ResearchRun.iter_session_inputs`
+reconstructs and verifies one original snapshot at a time; it does not query the
+latest temporal store. Do not materialize every reconstructed prefix at once for
+large runs. Evaluation uses one full prefix at a time and passes only the last
+raw scores to the existing `simulate_history(..., evaluated_scores=...)` kernel.
+This optional research-only input does not grant any data/forecast/approval authority.
+
+Each consumed TemporalObservation's schema and manifest identity is now checked
+before projection. `observation_evidence_hashes` bind record identities/content.
+Caller group dictionaries must match canonical per-period classification
+observations in that period's pinned manifest. The current version does not
+infer classification validity from a nonblank label or from today's sector map.
+Group simulation settings require an explicit `neutralization_group_field` in
+the research spec (and the momentum template), for example `sector`.
+
+The journal bounds encoded input changes at 256 MiB. Exceeding this budget is an
+explicit failure, not truncation or permission to drop evidence. Retained evidence
+scales with incoming cells and actual revisions; full-prefix CPU evaluation and
+caller-owned reference/session structures remain separate optimization work.
